\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


Topology optimization changes the material region to improve an objective subject to state equations. A level-set function encodes that region by a sublevel set. Adaptive meshes refine or coarsen the numerical discretization where error or geometric complexity requires it.
\paragraph{Record scope and qualifications.}
The catalogue title is retained as metadata. Named certificates, contracts, bounds or frameworks in that title are not asserted as results of the original source extract.
The bundle lists several method-design goals without fixed state equations, error bounds, or global-optimality requirements.

Source-record limitation: A bundle of numerical-design goals lacks precise correctness, approximation, or complexity requirements.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For adaptive topology optimization using level-set and state-variable discretizations, determine reliable refinement and coarsening strategies, methods for escaping local minima, efficient hierarchical B-spline gradient schemes, couplings with isogeometric shape optimization, and algorithms for extracting surface or volume parametrizations from the level-set field. \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2019/33}{[S2]}
